fields.doc:
`orgs/{org}/projects/{project}/envs/{env}/organization_roles/{organization_role}`;
the final segment is the role key memberships name, for example
`hr_manager`.

`accepted` (recorded now), `duplicate` (already recorded with the same
content: a no-op), `conflict` (its key was recorded with other content;
this one is never counted) or `rejected` (refused; see `reason`).

messages.doc:
An Error Group is the deterministic grouping of error occurrences by
fingerprint. Acknowledge, resolve, and reopen require the current etag;
occurrences are immutable.

A Runner is one runner: one machine for exactly one job, on its own
Sandboxes lease, released and wiped after. Runners is its only writer;
callers read it.

fields.doc:
The worker container: its image, command, env and instance type.
`timeout` is the longest one worker lives, so the pool turns over;
`max_retries` and `concurrency` do not apply.

methods.doc:
Sends a user message. On an idle or failed session it starts a new turn;
while a turn runs it is refused with `INVALID_STATE` (use `:steer`).
The same `Idempotency-Key` returns the same event.
